<!-- ID: executive_summary -->
Package 1.2 is BLOCKED pending stronger regression proof for the claimed container-aware corpus. The implementation correctly introduces `DocumentContext` and a provider interface, reuses `parse_frontmatter`, keeps `markdown-it-py` behind the provider seam with a deterministic local fallback, and preserves the public `manage_docs(action="quality_check")` path. Required focused tests all pass, plus adjacent scaffold-quality tests. The blocking issue is evidence quality: the new regression test fixture contains blockquote, list, table, inline-code, and indented-code examples, but it does not assert behavior for those cases, so the package does not yet prove criterion 6 or the checklist claim that the fence and container corpus is covered.
